{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QGameOfLife","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QGameOfLife","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qGameOfLife_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qGameOfLife_stable","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.lean#L68-L89","doc":"**Stability (non-degeneracy).** The q-AND amplitude carries a nonzero\n`(q − 1)` factor, so it is a nonzero element of `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`: the\nevolution is non-degenerate.\n\nReplaces the former `axiom qGameOfLife_stable_axiom`, which *trusted* this\nglobally. The unused `q > 1` substrate hypotheses are dropped — `q − 1 ≠ 0`\nholds unconditionally in `R_q` (the indeterminate minus a constant is a\nnonzero Laurent polynomial). Discharged **sorry-free** via the injective\nring hom `Polynomial.toLaurent`: `q − 1 = toLaurent (X − 1)` and `X − 1 ≠ 0`\nin `ℤ[X]`, so injectivity gives `q − 1 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qGameOfLife_unitary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qGameOfLife_unitary","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.lean#L62-L66","doc":"**Unitarity ⇒ bijectivity.** A unitary q-Toffoli gate is bijective, hence\nso is the q-GoL tick. *Derived* from the gate's bijectivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qGameOfLife_reversible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qGameOfLife_reversible","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.lean#L55-L60","doc":"**Reversibility.** Each q-Toffoli gate is its own inverse (an involution\nin `H₃(q)` under the Markov-trace dagger involution), so the q-GoL tick is\nreversible. *Derived* from the gate's involutivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qGameOfLife","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qGameOfLife","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.lean#L48-L53","doc":"**The q-Game of Life tick** on a lattice config space `L`: one application\nof a q-Toffoli gate `T` (ancilla-encoded neighbour sums realising Conway's\nsurvival/birth rules). Parameterised by the gate `T` so that the tick's\nreversibility/unitarity are *derived* from the gate's properties — not\nasserted of `id`. Label: prop:q-game-of-life. Ref: [pena2022] ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-game-of-life","label":"prop:q-game-of-life","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qAnd_amplitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qAnd_amplitude","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.lean#L42-L46","doc":"The q-AND amplitude Φ(q) = (q-1)(q^(3/2)+q^(1/2)-1)(q^(3/2)+q+1)/(2(q+1)²).\nParameterised via a Laurent polynomial proxy (placeholder for the\nfractional-power expression); the leading `(q-1)` factor is the part\nthat controls non-degeneracy. Ref: prop:toffoli-transfer-matrix ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.q_param","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.lean#L38-L40","doc":"The substrate indeterminate `q ∈ R_q` (the canonical\n`LaurentPolynomial.T 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.R_q","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-game-of-life.lean#L33-L36","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ), matching the\nrepeated local convention across the QOU tree (`CategoricalDqSquared`,\n`Hecke.MarkovTraceProduct`, `Archimedean.GroundRing`, …). ","signatureChunk":0}]}